{"t": 1793318762514, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "wall_lantern", "Walls: scrubbed logs turn warm dark brown, grimy logs stay pale grey; distinguishable up close, from a step back, and with the lantern lit (contrast a bit lower under the warm lantern). But 'Scrub the walls' is slow: each reach-sized patch adds ~1% of wallsClean (~2 checklist %) for ~2 s of scrubbing, plus repositioning since reach is short and 'Too far to reach' triggers often while strafing along a wall. 13% -> 26% took ticks 5600-9980 (~146 game s, ~60 s of it actual scrubbing). Extrapolated: ~10+ game minutes of strafe-and-scrub to reach 100%."]}
